# Dependencies left out of a package base: it is built without the optional
# feature they bring, never waits for them and does not require them.
# base<TAB>dependency<TAB>what is left out
# The dependency is an Arch package name (the recipe's depends) or a package
# base (arch/needs), each given where they differ (hip-runtime-amd of
# hip-runtime). A package of the base itself named here is not made.
plasma-nm	qt6-webengine	the Cisco AnyConnect VPN sign-in page
kdeplasma-addons	qt6-webengine	the dictionary and web browser applets
plasma-desktop	kaccounts-integration	the OpenDesktop integration plugin
purpose	kaccounts-integration	the Nextcloud and ownCloud sharing plugins
# GPU compute (CUDA, ROCm/HIP: arch/long), built without; arch/fixes turns it off
openucx	cuda	the CUDA transports
openucx	rocm-language-runtime	the ROCm transports
openucx	rocm-hip-sdk	the ROCm transports (rocm-language-runtime's base)
openucc	cuda	the CUDA execution engine and transport
openucc	nccl	the NCCL transport
openucc	hip-runtime-amd	the ROCm execution engine
openucc	hip-runtime	the ROCm execution engine (hip-runtime-amd's base)
openucc	rocm-llvm	the ROCm execution engine (its HIP compiler)
openucc	rccl	the RCCL transport
openmpi	cuda	CUDA-aware MPI
openmpi	nvidia-utils	nothing more: it was there for CUDA's libcuda.so
openmpi	hip-runtime-amd	ROCm-aware MPI
openmpi	hip-runtime	ROCm-aware MPI (hip-runtime-amd's base)
openimagedenoise	cuda	the CUDA device (NVIDIA GPUs)
openimagedenoise	hip-runtime-amd	the HIP device (AMD GPUs)
openimagedenoise	hip-runtime	the HIP device (hip-runtime-amd's base)
adios2	cuda	CUDA buffers
opencv	cuda	the CUDA modules
opencv	cudnn	the CUDA modules (cuDNN for dnn)
opencv	opencv-cuda	the CUDA build of OpenCV
opencv	python-opencv-cuda	the CUDA build of OpenCV
# qt6-webengine is built apart (arch/long); what needs it only for an extra
pyside6	qt6-webengine	the QtWebEngine bindings (PySide builds the modules Qt has)
pyside6	qt6-webview	the QtWebView bindings
hspell	qt6-webengine	hunspell-he's dictionaries for Qt WebEngine (.bdic)
# Documentation tools built early (a minimal build), so that what generates
# documentation with them can wait for them: doxygen, graphviz and gi-docgen
# (with python-pygments) were in the big cycle through qt6, llvm, texlive...
doxygen	doxygen-docs	its manual (HTML and PDF: LaTeX, ghostscript and graphviz to make)
doxygen	texlive-texmf	nothing more: it was there for doxygen-docs (texlive-fontsrecommended's base)
doxygen	texlive-fontsrecommended	nothing more: it was there for doxygen-docs
doxygen	texlive-fontutils	nothing more: it was there for doxygen-docs
doxygen	texlive-latexextra	nothing more: it was there for doxygen-docs
doxygen	texlive-plaingeneric	nothing more: it was there for doxygen-docs
doxygen	ghostscript	nothing more: it was there for doxygen-docs
doxygen	graphviz	nothing more: it was there for doxygen-docs (dot is still used at run time when installed)
doxygen	qt6-base	doxywizard, the GUI front end
doxygen	qt6-svg	doxywizard, the GUI front end
doxygen	llvm	libclang parsing (CLANG_ASSISTED_PARSING)
doxygen	clang	libclang parsing (llvm's base)
doxygen	llvm-libs	libclang parsing (llvm's base)
doxygen	fmt	nothing: doxygen's bundled fmt is used (fmt waits for doxygen, mkdocs and npm)
doxygen	spdlog	nothing: doxygen's bundled spdlog is used (it needs fmt)
graphviz	pango	the cairo/pango renderers (PNG, PDF and the like; SVG, PostScript and the text formats stay)
graphviz	gd	the gd renderers (PNG, GIF, JPEG) and the gdtclft Tcl package
graphviz	librsvg	SVG images inside graphs (rsvg loader)
graphviz	ghostscript	PostScript images inside graphs (gs loader)
graphviz	gts	the sfdp overlap removal by GTS triangulation (sfdp itself stays)
graphviz	qt6-base	gvedit, the GUI editor
graphviz	swig	the gv language bindings (Python, Perl, Lua, Tcl gv...; tcldot and tclpathplan stay)
graphviz	mono	the C# bindings
graphviz	guile	the Guile bindings
graphviz	lua	the Lua bindings
graphviz	r	the R bindings
graphviz	tk	nothing: graphviz 16 has no Tk extension any more
python-pygments	python-sphinx	its HTML documentation (/usr/share/doc/python-pygments)
# wayland without its documentation (wayland-docs): built early, everything waits for it
wayland	doxygen	the documentation (wayland-docs)
wayland	graphviz	the documentation (wayland-docs)
wayland	xmlto	the documentation (wayland-docs)
wayland	docbook-xsl	the documentation (wayland-docs)
wayland	mdbook	the documentation (wayland-docs)
# sysprof needs glib2 (and gtk4...): glib2 comes first, built without it; arch/fixes turns it off
glib2	sysprof	sysprof's tracing marks (its capture library)
glib2	libsysprof-capture	sysprof's tracing marks (its capture library)
pulseaudio	libasyncns	asynchronous name lookups of the network modules (libasyncns: its Git host, git.0pointer.net, is gone; meson auto feature)
gtk-doc	dblatex	PDF output (gtkdoc-mkpdf: its meson.build finds dblatex and fop with required: false)
krb5	libldap	the LDAP database back end of the KDC (kdb5_ldap_util, libkdb_ldap): openldap needs libsasl, which needs krb5
krb5	openldap	the LDAP database back end (libldap's base)
qt6-base	mariadb-libs	the MariaDB/MySQL SQL driver (Qt's sql_mysql feature is found, not required)
qt6-base	mariadb	the MariaDB/MySQL SQL driver (mariadb-libs's base)
qt6-base	postgresql	the PostgreSQL SQL driver (sql_psql, found, not required)
qt6-base	freetds	the MS SQL driver (sql_tds, found, not required)
